00:11:08,856 --> 00:11:09,881
one percent.

283
00:11:10,061 --> 00:11:13,483
Their conclusion was that the price increases

284
00:11:13,483 --> 00:11:16,448
consumers see mostly reflect inflation,

285
00:11:16,448 --> 00:11:17,817
not tariffs alone.

286
00:11:17,997 --> 00:11:20,347
That is a more careful answer than

287
00:11:20,347 --> 00:11:21,660
the headlines gave,

288
00:11:21,660 --> 00:11:23,941
and it is worth taking seriously.

289
00:11:24,291 --> 00:11:26,133
But we should be careful not to

290
00:11:26,133 --> 00:11:27,322
overstate it either.

291
00:11:27,502 --> 00:11:31,442
The same analysis covers only popular trims,

292
00:11:31,442 --> 00:11:34,665
not base trims or fully loaded ones.

293
00:11:34,845 --> 00:11:37,930
It calls itself dramatically simplified,

294
00:11:37,930 --> 00:11:40,397
and it does not separate out raw

295
00:11:40,397 --> 00:11:42,556
material costs, trade deals,

296
00:11:42,556 --> 00:11:45,487
financing costs or where the truck was

297
00:11:45,487 --> 00:11:46,258
assembled.

298
00:11:46,438 --> 00:11:49,558
And Cox Automotive's industry data tells a

299
00:11:49,558 --> 00:11:51,638
different part of the story,

300
00:11:51,638 --> 00:11:54,832
with thirty billion dollars in tariff costs

301
00:11:54,832 --> 00:11:58,175
and imported vehicles costing thousands more.

302
00:11:58,355 --> 00:12:00,259
Both can be true at once.

303
00:12:00,609 --> 00:12:01,991
Now the averages.

304
00:12:02,171 --> 00:12:04,599
According to Kelley Blue Book,

305
00:12:04,599 --> 00:12:08,484
the average full-size pickup sold for sixty-five

306
00:12:08,484 --> 00:12:12,531
thousand, nine hundred sixty-four dollars in March

307
00:12:12,531 --> 00:12:14,231
of twenty twenty-six,

308
00:12:14,231 --> 00:12:16,417
up two point eight percent.

309
00:12:16,597 --> 00:12:19,482
By August it was sixty-seven thousand,

310
00:12:19,482 --> 00:12:21,835
four hundred forty-six dollars,

311
00:12:21,835 --> 00:12:24,189
up two point one percent from a

312
00:12:24,189 --> 00:12:25,176
year earlier.

313
00:12:25,356 --> 00:12:27,697
Those are transaction prices,

314
00:12:27,697 --> 00:12:30,925
which include what buyers actually paid,

315
00:12:30,925 --> 00:12:31,974
with options.

316
00:12:32,154 --> 00:12:34,871
They are much higher than the trims

317
00:12:34,871 --> 00:12:36,190
in the TFL study,

318
00:12:36,190 --> 00:12:39,606
because buyers tend to choose more expensive

319
00:12:39,606 --> 00:12:40,304
versions.

320
00:12:40,654 --> 00:12:42,466
One more thing that matters.

321
00:12:42,646 --> 00:12:46,673
Cox Automotive reported that incentives were six

322
00:12:46,673 --> 00:12:49,944
point five percent of the average price

323
00:12:49,944 --> 00:12:52,965
in August, down from seven point two

324
00:12:52,965 --> 00:12:54,894
percent a year earlier.

325
00:12:55,074 --> 00:12:58,516
So discounts got smaller while prices rose

326
00:12:58,516 --> 00:12:59,254
a little.

327
00:12:59,434 --> 00:13:01,829
That is the real squeeze on a

328
00:13:01,829 --> 00:13:02,325
buyer.

329
00:13:02,505 --> 00:13:04,443
It is not one big jump.

330
00:13:04,623 --> 00:13:06,855
It is several small changes,

331
00:13:06,855 --> 00:13:08,210
a higher sticker,

332
00:13:08,210 --> 00:13:10,203
a higher destination fee,

333
00:13:10,203 --> 00:13:12,036
and a smaller discount,

334
00:13:12,036 --> 00:13:14,666
all moving in the same direction.

335
00:13:15,016 --> 00:13:17,581
And the tariffs themselves have no end

336
00:13:17,581 --> 00:13:17,919
date.

337
00:13:18,099 --> 00:13:19,725
According to CBT News,

338
00:13:19,725 --> 00:13:22,831
the tariffs were imposed under Section two

339
00:13:22,831 --> 00:13:25,788
thirty-two of the Trade Expansion Act of

340
00:13:25,788 --> 00:13:28,967
nineteen sixty-two, and they do not include

341
00:13:28,967 --> 00:13:30,150
a sunset clause.

342
00:13:30,330 --> 00:13:33,794
Changing them would need administrative action or

343
00:13:33,794 --> 00:13:35,137
legal intervention.

344
00:13:35,317 --> 00:13:37,407
So if you are waiting for prices

345
00:13:37,407 --> 00:13:39,954
to drop because tariffs will disappear,

346
00:13:39,954 --> 00:13:42,632
the published reporting does not give you

347
00:13:42,632 --> 00:13:43,873
a date to wait for.

348
00:13:44,223 --> 00:13:46,245
Let's line the five trucks up,

349
00:13:46,245 --> 00:13:48,267
in dollars, so you can see the

350
00:13:48,267 --> 00:13:49,750
whole picture at once.

351
00:13:49,930 --> 00:13:52,853
The Silverado LT rose six thousand,

352
00:13:52,853 --> 00:13:55,526
two hundred ninety-five dollars.

353
00:13:55,706 --> 00:13:59,035
The Sierra SLE rose six thousand,

354
00:13:59,035 --> 00:14:00,245
ninety-five.

355
00:14:00,425 --> 00:14:04,003
The F-one-fifty XLT rose two thousand,

356
00:14:04,003 --> 00:14:06,451
nine hundred seventy-five.

357
00:14:06,631 --> 00:14:09,601
The Ram Big Horn rose two thousand,

358
00:14:09,601 --> 00:14:11,554
nine hundred sixty-two.

359
00:14:11,734 --> 00:14:14,865
And the Tacoma SR5 rose two hundred

360
00:14:14,865 --> 00:14:15,402
sixty.

361
00:14:15,582 --> 00:14:16,694
Same two years,

362
00:14:16,694 --> 00:14:19,215
same tariffs, and a spread of more

363
00:14:19,215 --> 00:14:22,551
than six thousand dollars between the highest

364
00:14:22,551 --> 00:14:23,663
and the lowest.

365
00:14:24,012 --> 00:14:26,524
That spread is the most important number

366
00:14:26,524 --> 00:14:27,403
in this video.

367
00:14:27,583 --> 00:14:30,524
If tariffs were the only reason prices

368
00:14:30,524 --> 00:14:33,310
rose, all of these trucks would move

369
00:14:33,310 --> 00:14:34,626
in a similar way,

370
00:14:34,626 --> 00:14:37,567
because they all face a similar system

371
00:14:37,567 --> 00:14:38,264
of costs.

372
00:14:38,444 --> 00:14:39,442
But they do not.

373
00:14:39,622 --> 00:14:42,363
The spread tells you that each company

374
00:14:42,363 --> 00:14:44,888
made its own choices about how much

375
00:14:44,888 --> 00:14:47,052
to charge, how much to absorb,

376
00:14:47,052 --> 00:14:49,433
and how much to add through fees.

377
00:14:49,613 --> 00:14:51,238
The tariff is the same.

378
00:14:51,418 --> 00:14:53,113
The decision is different.

379
00:14:53,463 --> 00:14:55,263
There is a second lesson in the

380
00:14:55,263 --> 00:14:56,076
dealer number.

381
00:14:56,256 --> 00:14:59,020
Cox said dealers absorbed four and a

382
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:01,631
half percent of the cost pressure.

383
00:15:01,811 --> 00:15:04,151
That means that at the dealership,

384
00:15:04,151 --> 00:15:06,628
there is real money that someone has

385
00:15:06,628 --> 00:15:08,417
already agreed to give up.

386
00:15:08,597 --> 00:15:10,595
And it means that a buyer who

387
00:15:10,595 --> 00:15:12,662
asks for a better price is not

388
00:15:12,662 --> 00:15:14,867
asking for something impossible.

389
00:15:15,047 --> 00:15:17,171
The cost is already being shared.

390
00:15:17,351 --> 00:15:19,637
The only question is who shares it

391
00:15:19,637 --> 00:15:20,242
with you.

392
00:15:20,592 --> 00:15:22,520
And here is what you should not

393
00:15:22,520 --> 00:15:24,261
conclude from these numbers.

394
00:15:24,441 --> 00:15:27,277
You should not conclude that tariffs did

395
00:15:27,277 --> 00:15:30,397
nothing, because the industry data says they

396
00:15:30,397 --> 00:15:33,091
added thirty billion dollars in costs.

397
00:15:33,271 --> 00:15:36,101
You should not conclude that a Silverado

398
00:15:36,101 --> 00:15:37,163
is a bad truck,

399
00:15:37,163 --> 00:15:40,701
because price and quality are different questions.

400
00:15:40,881 --> 00:15:43,395
And you should not conclude that the

401
00:15:43,395 --> 00:15:45,001
Tacoma will stay cheap,

402
00:15:45,001 --> 00:15:47,863
because a price in twenty twenty-six does

403
00:15:47,863 --> 00:15:50,866
not promise a price in twenty twenty-seven.

404
00:15:51,046 --> 00:15:53,021
Prices can change again,

405
00:15:53,021 --> 00:15:54,668
in either direction.

406
00:15:55,017 --> 00:15:57,489
So here are the questions to bring

407
00:15:57,489 --> 00:15:58,362
to a dealer,

408
00:15:58,362 --> 00:15:59,452
in plain words.

409
00:15:59,632 --> 00:16:01,512
What is the full price,

410
00:16:01,512 --> 00:16:02,738
with every fee,

411
00:16:02,738 --> 00:16:03,800
before taxes?

412
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:06,273
What is the destination charge,

413
00:16:06,273 --> 00:16:08,197
and is it the same as last

414
00:16:08,197 --> 00:16:08,566
year?

415
00:16:08,746 --> 00:16:11,828
Which incentives apply to this exact truck,

416
00:16:11,828 --> 00:16:13,332
and when do they end?

417
00:16:13,512 --> 00:16:15,352
And what would the price be at

418
00:16:15,352 --> 00:16:17,436
another dealer, for the same trim?

419
00:16:17,616 --> 00:16:20,326
Four questions, and any honest dealer can

420
00:16:20,326 --> 00:16:21,912
answer them in a minute.

421
00:16:22,262 --> 00:16:25,165
Finally, think about the five year picture.

422
00:16:25,345 --> 00:16:27,913
A truck that costs more to buy

423
00:16:27,913 --> 00:16:30,396
can still cost less to own if

424
00:16:30,396 --> 00:16:32,622
it holds its value better,

425
00:16:32,622 --> 00:16:33,906
uses less fuel,

426
00:16:33,906 --> 00:16:35,875
or needs fewer repairs.

427
00:16:36,055 --> 00:16:38,347
We will cover that in a future

428
00:16:38,347 --> 00:16:39,875
video, with numbers.

429
00:16:40,055 --> 00:16:42,144
For now, the lesson is that the

430
00:16:42,144 --> 00:16:44,570
sticker price is the first number in

431
00:16:44,570 --> 00:16:45,379
a long list,

432
00:16:45,379 --> 00:16:48,075
and the truck that looks expensive today

433
00:16:48,075 --> 00:16:50,231
is not always the one that costs

434
00:16:50,231 --> 00:16:51,108
you the most.

435
00:16:51,457 --> 00:16:53,965
Let's slow down and turn the biggest

436
00:16:53,965 --> 00:16:56,334
number into something you can use.

437
00:16:56,514 --> 00:17:00,415
A twelve point six percent increase sounds

438
00:17:00,415 --> 00:17:01,250
abstract.

439
00:17:01,430 --> 00:17:03,718
But for the Silverado LT it means

440
00:17:03,718 --> 00:17:07,254
six thousand, two hundred ninety-five dollars more,

441
00:17:07,254 --> 00:17:10,097
on a truck that cost forty-nine thousand,

442
00:17:10,097 --> 00:17:13,633
nine hundred ninety-five dollars two years earlier.

443
00:17:13,813 --> 00:17:15,385
If you finance a truck,

444
00:17:15,385 --> 00:17:17,710
that extra money does not just sit

445
00:17:17,710 --> 00:17:18,735
on the sticker.

446
00:17:18,915 --> 00:17:20,649
It becomes a bigger loan,

447
00:17:20,649 --> 00:17:22,868
and a bigger loan means a bigger

448
00:17:22,868 --> 00:17:25,225
payment every month for as long as

449
00:17:25,225 --> 00:17:26,543
you keep the truck.

450
00:17:26,892 --> 00:17:29,470
Now compare two figures from the same

451
00:17:29,470 --> 00:17:29,818
list.

452
00:17:29,998 --> 00:17:32,932
The Silverado went up twelve point six

453
00:17:32,932 --> 00:17:34,863
percent before inflation,

454
00:17:34,863 --> 00:17:38,183
and five point two percent after inflation.

455
00:17:38,363 --> 00:17:41,499
The difference between those two numbers is

456
00:17:41,499 --> 00:17:44,416
what everything cost in general over two

457
00:17:44,416 --> 00:17:44,853
years.

458
00:17:45,033 --> 00:17:47,704
So if a salesperson says prices are

459
00:17:47,704 --> 00:17:49,688
up because of the economy,

460
00:17:49,688 --> 00:17:51,291
part of that is true.

461
00:17:51,471 --> 00:17:53,651
But only five point two points of

462
00:17:53,651 --> 00:17:56,359
the Silverado increase are left after you

463
00:17:56,359 --> 00:17:58,077
take the general rise out.

464
00:17:58,257 --> 00:18:00,267
Always ask which of the two numbers

465
00:18:00,267 --> 00:18:01,415
you are being shown.

466
00:18:01,764 --> 00:18:04,309
A common mistake is to compare the

467
00:18:04,309 --> 00:18:07,527
monthly payment between two trucks and stop

468
00:18:07,527 --> 00:18:07,976
there.

469
00:18:08,156 --> 00:18:10,841
A payment can look the same because

470
00:18:10,841 --> 00:18:12,299
the loan is longer,

471
00:18:12,299 --> 00:18:15,215
or because the down payment is bigger.

472
00:18:15,395 --> 00:18:17,718
The number that does not hide anything

473
00:18:17,718 --> 00:18:19,307
is the out-the-door price.

474
00:18:19,487 --> 00:18:22,419
That is the price with the destination

475
00:18:22,419 --> 00:18:25,428
charge, every dealer fee and the taxes,

476
00:18:25,428 --> 00:18:26,662
all in one line.

477
00:18:26,842 --> 00:18:28,405
Ask for it in writing,

478
00:18:28,405 --> 00:18:30,890
for each truck you are considering,

479
00:18:30,890 --> 00:18:33,589
and compare those lines instead of the

480
00:18:33,589 --> 00:18:34,725
monthly payment.

481
00:18:35,075 --> 00:18:36,843
There is a second mistake,

482
00:18:36,843 --> 00:18:39,290
and it is comparing the wrong trims.

483
00:18:39,470 --> 00:18:42,552
The Tacoma SR5 at thirty-nine thousand,

484
00:18:42,552 --> 00:18:46,029
four hundred fifty dollars and the Silverado

485
00:18:46,029 --> 00:18:48,005
LT at fifty-six thousand,

486
00:18:48,005 --> 00:18:51,324
two hundred ninety dollars are not rivals.

487
00:18:51,504 --> 00:18:53,868
One is a midsize truck and the

488
00:18:53,868 --> 00:18:55,997
other is a full-size truck.

489
00:18:56,177 --> 00:18:58,099
If you are cross-shopping,

490
00:18:58,099 --> 00:19:00,464
put the Tacoma next to a midsize

491
00:19:00,464 --> 00:19:03,052
truck and the Silverado next to the

492
00:19:03,052 --> 00:19:04,826
F-one-fifty and the Ram.

493
00:19:05,006 --> 00:19:07,751
The study itself warns that its trims

494
00:19:07,751 --> 00:19:09,086
are not identical,

495
00:19:09,086 --> 00:19:12,053
and you should treat your own comparison

496
00:19:12,053 --> 00:19:13,017
the same way.

497
00:19:13,367 --> 00:19:15,829
So who does each result suit?

498
00:19:16,009 --> 00:19:18,766
If you want a full-size truck and

499
00:19:18,766 --> 00:19:20,605
care about price paid,

500
00:19:20,605 --> 00:19:23,530
the F-one-fifty XLT and the Ram Big

501
00:19:23,530 --> 00:19:26,287
Horn both rose about six percent,

502
00:19:26,287 --> 00:19:29,964
and both went slightly down after inflation.

503
00:19:30,144 --> 00:19:32,804
If you only need a smaller truck,

504
00:19:32,804 --> 00:19:35,383
the Tacoma SR5 moved by just two

505
00:19:35,383 --> 00:19:37,156
hundred sixty dollars.

506
00:19:37,336 --> 00:19:39,016
And if you are set on a

507
00:19:39,016 --> 00:19:40,623
Silverado or a Sierra,

508
00:19:40,623 --> 00:19:43,837
the numbers say you should negotiate harder,

509
00:19:43,837 --> 00:19:46,393
because those two rose the most and

510
00:19:46,393 --> 00:19:49,096
the dealers absorbed part of the cost

511
00:19:49,096 --> 00:19:50,630
in the industry data.

512
00:19:50,980 --> 00:19:52,152
And who should wait?

513
00:19:52,332 --> 00:19:54,923
If your current truck is running well

514
00:19:54,923 --> 00:19:57,024
and your only reason to buy is

515
00:19:57,024 --> 00:19:58,985
fear of the next price rise,

516
00:19:58,985 --> 00:20:01,016
the numbers do not force you.

517
00:20:01,196 --> 00:20:03,734
The tariffs have no sunset clause,

518
00:20:03,734 --> 00:20:06,122
so waiting for them to vanish is

519
00:20:06,122 --> 00:20:07,466
not a plan either.

520
00:20:07,646 --> 00:20:09,566
What you can do is compare the

521
00:20:09,566 --> 00:20:11,359
same trim on the same day at

522
00:20:11,359 --> 00:20:12,703
more than one dealer,

523
00:20:12,703 --> 00:20:14,111
write the prices down,

524
00:20:14,111 --> 00:20:16,864
and let the difference between them decide.

525
00:20:17,044 --> 00:20:19,567
A calm buyer with three quotes has

526
00:20:19,567 --> 00:20:22,165
more power than a rushed buyer with

527
00:20:22,165 --> 00:20:22,536
none.

528
00:20:22,885 --> 00:20:24,882
So what should you check before you

529
00:20:24,882 --> 00:20:26,879
buy a truck in twenty twenty-seven?

530
00:20:27,059 --> 00:20:29,822
First, compare the exact trim,

531
00:20:29,822 --> 00:20:31,111
not the model.

532
00:20:31,291 --> 00:20:34,432
A fifty-six thousand dollar Silverado and a

533
00:20:34,432 --> 00:20:38,667
fifty-two thousand dollar F-one-fifty are different trucks

534
00:20:38,667 --> 00:20:40,347
with different options.

535
00:20:40,527 --> 00:20:43,432
Second, ask for the destination fee in

536
00:20:43,432 --> 00:20:46,413
writing, and compare it between brands.

537
00:20:46,593 --> 00:20:48,072
It can be two thousand,

538
00:20:48,072 --> 00:20:50,258
seven hundred ninety-five dollars,

539
00:20:50,258 --> 00:20:52,252
and it is added after the price

540
00:20:52,252 --> 00:20:53,281
you were quoted.

541
00:20:53,630 --> 00:20:56,397
Third, look at the price after inflation,

542
00:20:56,397 --> 00:20:57,814
not only the sticker,

543
00:20:57,814 --> 00:20:59,905
if you are comparing a truck to

544
00:20:59,905 --> 00:21:01,862
the one you bought years ago.

545
00:21:02,042 --> 00:21:04,052
Fourth, ask about incentives,

546
00:21:04,052 --> 00:21:06,548
because they are smaller than a year

547
00:21:06,548 --> 00:21:06,825
ago.

548
00:21:07,005 --> 00:21:09,198
And fifth, do not assume that the

549
00:21:09,198 --> 00:21:11,921
brand with the biggest price increase has

550
00:21:11,921 --> 00:21:12,984
the worst truck.

551
00:21:13,164 --> 00:21:15,289
Price is a company decision.

552
00:21:15,469 --> 00:21:17,720
Quality is a different question,

553
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:19,759
and you can only answer it by

554
00:21:19,759 --> 00:21:21,518
checking the exact model.

555
00:21:21,867 --> 00:21:23,703
We put all of this into a

556
00:21:23,703 --> 00:21:27,742
checklist, the Twenty Twenty-Seven Truck Buyer's Guide.

557
00:21:27,922 --> 00:21:30,126
It covers the numbers to check,

558
00:21:30,126 --> 00:21:32,259
the questions to ask a dealer,

559
00:21:32,259 --> 00:21:34,819
and the warning signs we just walked

560
00:21:34,819 --> 00:21:35,387
through.

561
00:21:35,567 --> 00:21:37,696
The link is in the description and

562
00:21:37,696 --> 00:21:39,074
in the pinned comment.

563
00:21:39,254 --> 00:21:41,098
If you want to know what it

564
00:21:41,098 --> 00:21:43,216
